Let rosapi describe messages with ROS 2 sequence fields on Foxy (JetPack 5 image).

Symptom: rosbridge clients such as Foxglove cannot show camera topics, because
rosapi's message-definition lookup fails for sensor_msgs/Image and
CompressedImage.

Cause: ROS 2 reports variable-length array fields as sequence<T>, for example
sequence<uint8> for image data. Foxy's rosapi only understands the ROS 1 form
T[], so it treats sequence<uint8> as a message type and fails to load it.

Fix: read sequence<T> as element type T with variable length (arraylen 0).
Upstream fixed this in rosbridge_suite 2.0.0 (RobotWebTools/rosbridge_suite#883,
2023), after Foxy's last release. Delete this patch when the Foxy image is
retired. Dockerfile.jetson-jp5 applies it and asserts both image types resolve.

--- a/objectutils.py
+++ b/objectutils.py
@@ -150,6 +150,10 @@
         # Pull out the type and determine whether it's an array
         field_type = instance._fields_and_field_types[name[1:]]  # Remove trailing underscore.
         arraylen = -1
+        # ROS 2 represents variable arrays as sequence<T>, not only T[].
+        if field_type.startswith("sequence<") and field_type.endswith(">"):
+            field_type = field_type[9:-1].split(",", 1)[0].strip()
+            arraylen = 0
         if field_type[-1:] == "]":
             if field_type[-2:-1] == "[":
                 arraylen = 0
